# Bandit — Kindred's Newspaper Dog

Bandit is not a mascot. He is the face of Kindred: the loyal newspaper dog who
personally delivers every user's morning edition. Treat his design with the
same discipline as a real brand mark (Nike swoosh, Duolingo owl).

## Bandit v1.0 — approved and locked

The single source of truth is the **approved Bandit v1.0 master reference**,
`assets/bandit/v1/bandit-v1-master-reference.png` — matched to the real
Kindred app icon. His identity is frozen: head/muzzle/ear/patch/nose shape,
body/tail/leg proportions, line weight, color palette, expression, and gentle
smile never change. Only pose, body position, accessories, props, and small
in-character expression tweaks may vary.

His **Core Pose Library v1** lives in `assets/bandit/v1/` and is registered
in `BANDIT_ASSETS` (`lib/bandit/character.ts`): `reference`,
`standing-neutral`, `walking-newspaper` (his **signature pose**,
`BANDIT_SIGNATURE_POSE` — the primary illustration throughout Kindred),
`sitting`, `head-portrait`, `standing-no-newspaper`. The full approved
ten-pose reference sheet (adds lying down, waving, looking up, holding a
recommendation card, sleeping, reading the newspaper) is
`assets/bandit/v1/bandit-v1-pose-library-full.png`
(`BANDIT_POSE_LIBRARY_SHEET`) — generate matching individual production
assets from it before wiring any of those five poses into a real screen.

**Bandit v1.0 is permanently locked** — including body proportions (adult
athletic Jack Russell: longer legs, deeper chest, longer torso, smaller
head-to-body ratio). No further redesigns unless explicitly requested by the
user. Never reinterpret, restyle, or "improve" his design. To add a new surface
that needs a pose not yet in the library, generate it with the app icon +
`bandit-v1-master-reference.png` as reference images (strong visual
grounding, not description alone), register it in `BANDIT_ASSETS`, then use
it — don't improvise a pose inline. Earlier concept sheets and single-dog
drafts that predate v1.0 are superseded; never resurrect them as a reference.

**Build:** a mature adult dog (~3-5 years old) — never a puppy. Adult Jack
Russell proportions: longer muzzle, broader chest, stronger shoulders, longer
legs, confident grounded stance in every pose.

**Fixed markings (never change):**
- Warm white coat and face
- Two dark chocolate-brown floppy ears
- One warm golden-brown patch over his **RIGHT eye only** — large and
  soft-rounded, covering roughly one-third of the visible side of his face;
  his single most defining feature, matched to the official app icon
- Warm rich brown eyes, small relative to his head; dark chocolate-brown nose
  (same color as his ears)
- Kindred gold bandana around his neck
- Rolled newspaper (warm cream paper), often carried in his mouth

**Brand colors (never substitute):** Coat `#F8F8F6` · Eye patch `#B7772E` ·
Bandana `#D8A63A` · Ears/nose `#4A3326` · Eyes `#5A3E2B` · Newspaper `#F3E8CF`
· All outline/line-work `#1C2746`.

**Orientation rule:** in every side or three-quarter pose, Bandit faces
**screen-RIGHT** (matching the real app icon), so the cheek nearest the
viewer is correctly his right eye (and the patch). Never draw him facing
screen-left in profile. In a direct front-facing pose, the patch appears on
the **viewer's left** (mirror-correct for his own right eye).

**Hard rules:** always on all four paws · never anthropomorphic (no human
hands, no upright human posture) · never clothed beyond the bandana.

## Personality

Always: calm, friendly, dependable, intelligent, gentle, trustworthy, warm —
soft eyes, relaxed eyebrows, a gentle genuine smile, like a beloved
neighborhood dog. Never: hyper, silly, loud, chaotic, goofy, overly
cartoonish, or reading as a guard/working dog. Any copy voiced as Bandit
(Bandit's Pick intros, greetings, empty states) should read as one or two
quiet, simple sentences — never a joke, never exclamation-heavy.

## Using Bandit in the app

- Render Bandit only through `components/BanditCharacter.tsx`
  (`<BanditCharacter pose="..." />`), never by `require`-ing an asset path
  directly in a screen.
- Only use poses defined in `BanditPose` (`lib/bandit/character.ts`).
- Approved near-term surfaces: home screen (waiting beside today's paper, or
  his signature walking-with-newspaper pose), Bandit's Pick (`sitting` beside
  the featured recommendation), loading states (`walking-newspaper` instead
  of a spinner), pull-to-refresh (trots off, returns with a fresh paper),
  empty Saved/Clippings board (`sitting`), notifications/speech bubbles
  (`head-portrait`).
- Consistency over creativity — when in doubt, match the existing reference
  rather than adding a new stylistic flourish.
